{
  "schema": "raknor-v1.1-draft/fail-closed-policy-vectors/0.1",
  "proposal": "https://github.com/raknor-ai/agent-governance-standard/issues/3",
  "license": "CC0-1.0",
  "note": "Black-box: each vector is a policy state plus one requested action. Expected outcome is observable through the system API: whether the action executed, and whether a governance event (SC-OB-03) was emitted. Allowlist entries are exact action identifiers (namespace:name) or the single wildcard `*`; any other match-all spelling (\"all\", \"any\", a regex) is unrecognised, so the policy is indeterminate. A verdict object may carry `after_s` (when the approver answered) against the policy's `approver_deadline_s`: an explicit DENY before the deadline is a normal denial; no verdict by the deadline is indeterminate. Every indeterminate denial's event carries event_detail: which input was indeterminate, the value exactly as received (unnormalised), and its form (missing | null | empty | text | non_text). Value-as-received requirement from aigentical-ai, agentbaseline#49.",
  "vectors": [
    {
      "id": "a1-empty-allowlist",
      "clause": "a",
      "policy": {
        "allowlist": []
      },
      "action": "tool:shell.exec",
      "verdict": "ALLOW",
      "expect": {
        "executed": false,
        "event": "policy_indeterminate",
        "event_detail": {
          "input": "allowlist",
          "received_value": [],
          "received_form": "empty"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "a2-null-allowlist",
      "clause": "a",
      "policy": {
        "allowlist": null
      },
      "action": "tool:shell.exec",
      "verdict": "ALLOW",
